{
  "id": "lab-grades-the-pull-request-merge",
  "origin": "inventory",
  "behaviour": "The lab grades the same test merge commit GitHub Actions grades for a pull request. A pull request head event keeps the pull request number, 0 for every other event. Before it expands a pull request or hotfix grade that is not a plant, the scheduler resolves GitHub's test merge of that pull request and takes it only when the merge's second parent is the head; a refused or unanswered read, a failed fetch of the merge or its parents, a resolution still running past its own bound, or GitHub naming no merge yet each count as one try, held and tried again, and after UNMERGED_TRIES such tries the lab gives up and grades the bare head against its event base, remembered on the grade as a fallback whose required check names the bound and that it graded the head itself; a finished resolution, whatever it answered, waits for its own head while other heads are asked, forgotten an hour after it began when no head reads it; an absent answer or a failed resolution is then read once and forgotten, so every try reads GitHub again, while a found merge its head has read is kept and reused for a fresh window. The resolver reads GitHub by the owner and name of the repository address the scheduler names, and asks its mirror by that address. With a resolved merge, the graded commit's tree and files feed the static unit keys and the worker's checkout, the merge's first parent is the merge base its units diff against and the context's base, the grader revision stays the event's own base, and the head stays the head on every check run, lane and piece of evidence. A lease of such a grade carries the graded commit beside the head, base and grader; its worker reads github.sha as the graded commit and fetches it through a git bundle the scheduler serves when its own node mirror lacks the merge. The grade's identity includes the graded commit once resolved, so a rerequest after dev moved and a newer merge resolved grades under a new key, superseding its own older grade of the same head and merge; a grade with no resolved merge, or whose merge has not changed, keeps the key and the lane entry it already had. The summary of a grade carries its graded commit only once resolved and its fallback flag only once spent; every other grade carries neither. A grade's pull request number travels on its state, so a required-frame change that restarts a live pull request or hotfix grade resolves its merge again instead of silently falling back to the bare head; a restart whose merge resolution is still pending or failed holds for a later pass instead of raising out of the advance loop, its own count of tries kept on the grade document. Merge group, push, promotion and plant grades are unchanged. When a pull request or hotfix request resolves a merge, every other live pull request or hotfix grade of its head on a different commit, whatever its lane, is replaced the same way, carrying its unfinished jobs into the new grade, so a head announced twice, by a signed notice and by GitHub's own delivery, never holds two live grades. A notice naming no pull request yields, held nowhere, to a waiting pull request entry of its head or to a live grade of it already on a resolved merge, and a request naming a pull request number drops the waiting notice its head left behind in the other class.",
  "seam": "scripts.ci_lab.webhooks.head_events and head_data over a pull_request or rerequested check_run delivery, scripts.ci_lab.scheduler.Scheduler.tick over its fakes with a merges port that resolves, pends, refuses or finds no merge, scripts.ci_lab.scheduler.Scheduler._supersede over a rerequest of the same head with a newer merge, scripts.ci_lab.scheduler.MirrorExpander.expand and bundle over a real git repository, scripts.ci_lab.executors.static, tests and _context over a lease naming a graded commit, scripts.ci_lab.lease_api the /bundle route, scripts.ci_lab.merges.Background over a resolver that fails in every way and over several heads asked in turn, scripts.ci_lab.merges.Resolver over a repository address with a fake reader and with its default reader, and scripts.ci_lab.digests.grade_key over GradeInputs with a graded commit",
  "rules": [
    "lab-merge-reader-built-from-address",
    "lab-merge-keep-rule-reads-the-answer"
  ],
